= Daily Meals and Travel Per Diems

== The Individual Meal Allowance Framework

When traveling away from your regular office city on approved firm business, Noice & Toit LLP reimburses actual, necessary meal expenditures up to daily limits. Our philosophy focuses on providing wholesome, nourishing meals that support professional stamina while avoiding wasteful extravagance.

Reimbursement is based on actual receipts rather than flat untaxed cash allowances, in compliance with international tax statutory regimes. Employees must retain and upload itemized register receipts for all dining purchases.

== Daily Meal Allowance Caps

Daily meal thresholds are calibrated to reflect realistic business dining costs in metropolitan business centers. The limits cover food, non-alcoholic beverages, applicable sales taxes, and standard gratuities:

=== Individual Meal Thresholds
- *Breakfast*: Up to *€15.00* / *\$18.00* / *£13.00*.
  - *Eligibility*: Reimbursable only when travel begins before 07:00 AM local time, or when breakfast is not included in the booked hotel room rate.
- *Lunch*: Up to *€25.00* / *\$30.00* / *£22.00*.
  - *Eligibility*: Reimbursable when travel spans the standard midday lunch period (12:00 PM to 2:00 PM) away from the regular office.
- *Dinner*: Up to *€45.00* / *\$55.00* / *£38.00*.
  - *Eligibility*: Reimbursable when business travel extends past 7:00 PM local time.
- *Maximum Daily Aggregate Cap*: *€85.00* / *\$100.00* / *£73.00*.
  - The maximum allowable cumulative meal reimbursement across a single calendar day.

#card-do("Stay within daily meal spending caps")[
  Select quality, casual business dining that fits within our daily caps. While individual meal caps provide a useful benchmark, Finance evaluates compliance against the total daily limit of €85.00 / \$100.00.
]

#card-dont("Roll over unspent meal allowances")[
  Unspent meal allowances cannot be accumulated, carried over into subsequent days, or converted into cash reimbursements. If you spend €10 on lunch, your daily dinner cap remains €45.00, not €60.00.
]

== Alcohol on Individual Solo Travel

Noice & Toit LLP maintains an unambiguous, firm-wide policy regarding alcoholic beverages consumed during individual travel.

#card-dont("Claim alcoholic beverages during solo dining")[
  Alcoholic beverages (including beer, wine, cocktails, cider, and spirits) consumed while dining alone on business travel are strictly non-reimbursable. If your meal receipt includes an alcoholic beverage, you must circle that item, calculate the proportional tax, and deduct both the drink price and tax from your claimed total.
]

=== Auditing and Line-Item Reductions
Finance audits meal receipts for alcohol keywords (e.g., "IPA", "Merlot", "Pilsner", "Cocktail", "Spirits", "Wein"). If an itemized receipt contains alcohol and the employee failed to deduct it, Finance will automatically subtract the line item and recalculate the payout. If a traveler submits a summary credit card slip without itemization, Finance will assume the bill may contain unallowable items and reject the submission.

== Gratuities, Service Charges, and Local Tipping Norms

Tipping practices vary substantially across global jurisdictions. Gratuities are reimbursable when they align with established local customs:

=== North American Norms (United States and Canada)
- In restaurants where table service is provided, tips between 15% and 20% of the food and beverage subtotal are standard and fully reimbursable.
- Tips exceeding 20% are considered discretionary personal gifts and will be capped at 20% upon reimbursement.
- For quick-service counters and takeout coffee, discretionary tips exceeding \$1.00 are non-reimbursable.

=== European and United Kingdom Norms
- In European Union countries (including Germany, France, Italy, and Spain) and Switzerland, menu prices legally include value-added tax and service charges. Small discretionary cash or card tips (typically rounding up to the nearest euro or leaving 5% to 10%) are customary and reimbursable up to €5.00 per meal.
- In the United Kingdom, where an optional service charge (typically 12.5%) is automatically added to the restaurant bill, no additional tip should be added.
- Adding large North American-style 20% tips in Europe is non-compliant with firm policy; Finance will reduce the tip allowance to local statutory standards.

=== Asian and Middle Eastern Norms
- In Japan, South Korea, and Singapore, tipping is not customary and can cause offense. Do not leave tips in these countries. Where hotels or high-end dining rooms add a mandatory 10% service charge to the invoice, that charge is fully reimbursable.

== Conference Meals and Client-Provided Catering

When attending industry conferences, seminars, or client-hosted workshops where meals are provided as part of the event registration:
- Employees are expected to participate in the provided breakfast, lunch, or dinner.
- If you choose to dine at a commercial restaurant despite meals being fully provided at the event, that restaurant expense is non-reimbursable, unless an advance dietary or religious restriction prevented consumption of the provided catering.

== Grocery Purchases in Lieu of Dining Out

Employees staying in serviced apartments or desiring healthier dining options may purchase groceries (such as fresh fruit, bread, salad, and sandwich ingredients) from local supermarkets:
- Grocery purchases are reimbursable up to the daily meal cap (€85.00 / \$100.00) for the days covered by the stay.
- All personal care items, toiletries, household cleaning products, and alcoholic beverages purchased on the same supermarket receipt must be deducted before submission.

== Frequently Asked Questions

*Q: What if I am working late at my home office? Can I order dinner delivery?*\
A: When required to work in your regular office or home workspace past 8:30 PM on urgent client deliverables, you may claim an overtime meal delivery up to €20.00 / \$25.00 with manager sign-off. Alcohol is strictly excluded.

*Q: Can I buy snacks or coffee between meals?*\
A: Incidental coffee, tea, and snack purchases during travel are allowable, provided the cumulative cost of all breakfast, lunch, dinner, and snacks remains within the €85.00 / \$100.00 daily limit.
